FILED s526w2 (Opus, resumed s528 2026-10-25), from the Log-Log4perl-1.58 board census (t/025CustLevels.t stops after row 1, rc 2: Log/Log4perl/Logger.pm:731 `}) if (${Log::Log4perl::Level::LEVELS{$cust_prio}});`).  PRE-EXISTING (main 31cd8c02 = base /home/bernt/pcl).  LOUD (dies at run time).

    package P::Q; our %L = (5 => 'five'); our @A = (7, 8);
    package main;
    print "1 ", (${P::Q::L{5}} // 'U'), "\n";
    my %h = (k => 'v'); print "2 ", ${h{k}}, "\n";
    print "3 ", ${P::Q::A[1]}, "\n";
  perl 5.40.3: 1 five / 2 v / 3 8  (also `@{a[0,1]}` = the slice, `${ h{k} }` with spaces, a lexical %h, and as an lvalue `${h{new}} = 9`; no warning under `use warnings`)
  PCL: dies "Undefined subroutine &P::Q::L called" (and &main::h for the lexical)
  Probes scratch/s526w2/pbrace.pl pbrace2.pl.

PPI 1.291 builds the inner part as Word + Structure::Block (`{k}`) / Word + Structure::Constructor (`[2]`), not a Subscript -- so PCL's `_collapse_braced_bareword_derefs` (Pl/PExpr.pm, the `${name}` -> `$name` pre-pass) does not take it (its `_block_sole_bareword` wants ONE Word) and the Word becomes a call.  The fix is that pre-pass's sibling: Cast + Block holding exactly Word + {Block|Constructor} -> Symbol($sigil . word) + the subscript; whether the Block/Constructor must be re-built as a PPI::Structure::Subscript for the element machinery, or whether this belongs in the patched PPI (s527a's vendor/PPI: is it a PPI mis-structure? toke.c S_scan_ident treats `${ident[` / `${ident{` as the element spelling) is the first question -- NOT done in s526w2 because the PPI-at-source program (docs/ppi-fix-at-source-s527.md) owns new token/structure repairs.
ROWS: Log-Log4perl t/025CustLevels.t (*PLAN* "ran 1 of no plan") -- every custom-level path through Logger.pm:731.
